WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.040
- So you're not gonna believe

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:03.890
what the QShaman's lawyer
said in an interview,

00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:06.190
or you probably will believe what he said.

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:08.470
Albert Watkins, the
lawyer for the Qshaman,

00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:09.650
said, "A lot of these defendants,

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:11.270
and I'm going to use this colloquial term,

00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:12.320
perhaps disrespectfully,

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:14.150
but they're all (beep) short bus people.

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:15.389
These are people with brain damage.

00:00:15.389 --> 00:00:16.300
They're (beep).

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:17.610
They're on the (beep) spectrum."

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:19.540
Now, Watkins is an
incredibly infamous attorney

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:20.373
in his own right.

00:00:20.373 --> 00:00:22.217
The first line of his bio says that he is,

00:00:22.217 --> 00:00:24.210
"quite frankly, beyond description."

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:25.250
Now, I don't know if that's true,

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:27.050
but one description you might
not use is "good lawyer"

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:28.630
because just because
you're on the spectrum

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:29.820
doesn't mean you can't tell the difference

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:30.720
between right and wrong.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:32.480
So that's not a defense for
his client or anyone else,

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:35.050
and Watkins went on to say,
"They're part of our country.

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:35.883
They aren't bad people.

00:00:35.883 --> 00:00:37.470
They don't have a prior
criminal history (beep).

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.900
They were subjected to four-plus
years of (beep) propaganda,

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:41.500
the likes of which the world has not seen

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:42.530
since (beep) Hitler."

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:44.150
Interesting move to go after clemency

00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:45.720
while being about as
offensive as possible.

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:47.050
Now, that probably won't help

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:48.720
in terms of establishing guilt.

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:50.490
It might help in terms of sentencing

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:52.790
to try and get less
sentencing for the crimes

00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:54.160
that they will be convicted of.

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:56.240
But, you know, I guess you
defend the clients that you have,

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:57.520
not the clients that you want.

00:00:57.520 --> 00:01:00.003
So we will definitely
see all of them in court.

